Theorem RL-26: RC motion barriers (calls / IsShared / Set-SetTag)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-26 governs RC-motion barriers per Annex E §AIMS PRE-Style
      Global RC Motion: "RC motion SHALL NOT move RcInc(v)/RcDec(v) across
      RC-observable barriers FOR v: (a) calls passing v to an Owned or
      may_share=true parameter; (b) IsShared(v) (reads v's RC header); (c)
      Set/SetTag on v or any aggregate containing v (implicit field drops).
      Calls where v is NOT an argument (or Borrowed + no may_share) are
      transparent for v's motion. RcDec(v) additionally cannot move past any
      use of v or its aliases."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - RL-26 is the safety constraint on the RL-24/RL-25 PRE-style RC motion; a
      POST-PIPELINE pass over realized IR.

  Soundness property:
    Forall RcInc(v) / RcDec(v) and forall instruction I on the motion path:

      (P1) Barrier decision: motion of an RC op for v across I is BLOCKED iff I
           is (a) a call passing v to an Owned or may_share=true parameter, OR
           (b) IsShared(v), OR (c) Set/SetTag on v or an aggregate containing
           v. A call where v is not an argument (or Borrowed + no may_share)
           is transparent (motion permitted). RcDec(v) is additionally blocked
           from moving past any use of v.

      (P2) Soundness: each barrier OBSERVES v's reference count (a call to an
           Owned/may_share param may inc/dec it; IsShared reads the header;
           Set/SetTag triggers implicit field drops). Moving an RC op across
           such a barrier would change the count the barrier observes —
           changing observable behavior. A transparent instruction does not
           touch v's count, so motion across it preserves behavior.

    RL-26 is the constraint that makes RL-24/RL-25 RC motion behavior-
    preserving: motion is allowed only across instructions that cannot observe
    v's count.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the rc_counting engine.

    Part (P1/P2) — barrier-classification grid:
      call_owned_param_barrier -> blocked (a)
      isshared_barrier -> blocked (b)
      set_settag_barrier -> blocked (c)
      transparent_call_no_barrier -> NOT blocked (v not an argument)
      Coverage gate: 4 barrier cases. Negative-direction witness: motion across
      an IsShared(v) barrier must be blocked (it would change the count
      IsShared observes); RcDec(v) must not move past a use of v — both
      asserted.

    Engines dispatched:
      rc_counting (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl26_rc_motion_barriers;
        barrier-classification enumeration + IsShared / RcDec-past-use
        witnesses; emits Fail on a wrong barrier verdict)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 rc_counting engine discharges RL-26 via the RC-motion barrier grid (call-to-Owned/may_share / IsShared / Set-SetTag block motion because they observe v's count; a transparent call does not) with negative-direction witnesses for the IsShared barrier and the RcDec-past-use constraint, making RL-24/RL-25 motion behavior-preserving
